== Hybrid Vehicles

=== Definition and Technologies
A Hybrid Vehicle uses two or more power sources to move. The most common type is the Hybrid Electric Vehicle (HEV), using both an Internal Combustion Engine (ICE) and an electric motor.
- *Regenerative Braking:* Electric motor works as a generator during braking, converting braking energy into electricity stored in the battery.
- *Electric Motor Assist:* Electric motor helps the engine during acceleration and hill climbing, improving fuel efficiency.
- *Automatic Start/Stop System:* Engine automatically stops when the vehicle is at rest and restarts when the accelerator is pressed.

=== Types of Hybrid Vehicles
1. *Series Hybrid:* Electric motor alone drives the vehicle; ICE is used only to charge the battery.
2. *Parallel Hybrid:* Both electric motor and ICE drive the vehicle together.
3. *Series-Parallel Hybrid:* Vehicle can run on electric motor alone, ICE alone, or both combined.

=== Advantages and Disadvantages
- *Advantages:* Environment-friendly, better fuel economy, less dependence on fossil fuels, regenerative braking, lower running cost, and higher resale value.
- *Disadvantages:* Less power compared to conventional vehicles, high initial cost, higher maintenance cost, heavy battery weight, and high-voltage battery safety risks.

