*Q. Explain the principles of G2V (Grid-to-Vehicle) and V2G (Vehicle-to-Grid) systems. [4 Marks]*
- *Grid-to-Vehicle (G2V):* Electricity flows from the power grid to the EV battery via charging stations, usually during off-peak hours, to utilize surplus electricity and charge the vehicle.
- *Vehicle-to-Grid (V2G):* Electricity flows from the EV battery back to the power grid using a bidirectional charger during peak demand to balance supply and demand and improve grid stability.

