== International Climate Action

=== Recent Activities of Conference of the Parties (COP) in UNFCCC
The Conference of the Parties (COP) is the supreme decision-making body of the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (UNFCCC), held annually to address global climate change.
- *COP28 (Dubai, UAE, 2023):* Focused on the first Global Stocktake (GST); countries agreed to transition away from fossil fuels, triple global renewable energy capacity by 2030, and operationalize the Loss and Damage Fund.
- *COP29 (Baku, Azerbaijan, 2024):* Focused on climate finance for developing nations, advancing carbon market mechanisms, and transparency in climate reporting.
- *COP30 (Belém, Brazil, 2025):* Focused on strengthening climate action, updating NDCs, protecting forests and biodiversity, and accelerating the clean energy transition.
- *Key Areas Discussed:* Greenhouse gas emission reduction, renewable energy expansion, climate adaptation, financial support for developing countries, technology transfer, and ecosystem protection.